  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let&#39;s assume that the original position of the bubble is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;from one side of the ice cube of side&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>.</p><p>When the bubble is seen from one side, it can be written that</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>&#956;</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>For the view from the other side, it can be written that</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mi>&#956;</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>From equations (1) and (2), it is given that</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mn>24</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><mi>&#956;</mi></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>4</mn><mi>&#956;</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>&#8658;</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>24</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
